# Deny-by-default build context.
#
# The image contains the harness runtime only: its entry point, the package it
# imports and the hashed dependency lock. Everything else (git history, specs,
# tests, examples, datasets, eval reports, local logs, keys, editor swap files,
# archives) is excluded, so it cannot leak into a layer by accident.
*
!run_agent.py
!entrypoint.sh
!requirements.lock
!harness
!harness/**

# Explicit exclusions inside the whitelisted tree (last match wins).
harness/__pycache__
harness/**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so.dbg
**/answer.txt
**/solutions.json
**/trace.jsonl
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa*
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
